<title>ESTONIA: HOTEL OLUMPIA TURNOVER UP IN MAY.</title>
<headline>HOTEL OLUMPIA TURNOVER UP IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading hotel The Olumpia had net turnover of 19 million kroons in May compared to 16.3 million kroons in April, it said on Monday.</p>
<p>Some 85 percent of its rooms were filled in May compared to 75 percent in April, a hotel official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The privatisation agency is to sell 25.06 percent of Olumpia shares in a public offer for vouchers from June 30 to July 18.</p>
<p>The hotel's May profit figure will be ready by the middle of the month.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
